<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palma Cathedral</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1229">1229</a>–<a href="/years/1601">1601</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Cathedral of Santa Maria of Palma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palma">Palma</a> Cathedral is the Gothic cathedral of Palma on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a>, begun after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a> conquered the island in 1229 and built mainly between about 1300 and 1601 on the site of the city's main mosque. Rising above the sea wall, it has one of the tallest Gothic naves in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and its interior was remodelled by Antoni Gaudí in the early 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palma-cathedral.jpg" alt="Palma Cathedral" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Wolf, www.foto-tw.de · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathedrale_von_Palma_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
